Carafe: with CompactReturns and IndirectCallCache both on, an indirect call keeps only the cache check in line (the
record's guest RIP compared, its host code loaded, the push and the call). Filling an empty record and the lookup for
a call that misses the record go after the block's code and come back to the call. That moves about 60 bytes out of
the hot code at every indirect call site. The L1 lookup of the out-of-line pieces is shared by returns and calls.
MIT, as the files it changes.

